          "text": "; Consecution: sat exactly where the invariant holds of a state and fails after one step.\n; A model is a counterexample to induction for the kernel to check; unsat is not a verdict.\n; Inputs left out, whose types have no sort: failed, ret.spawn.\n(set-option :produce-models true)\n(set-logic ALL)\n\n; Records and variants.\n; A variant with the cases ok, waiting.\n(declare-datatype |variant:fda1d360| ((|variant:fda1d360#ok| (|variant:fda1d360#ok.value| Int)) (|variant:fda1d360#waiting|)))\n; {slot: <kind: ok: {value: Int} | waiting: {}>}\n(declare-datatype |record:a473073e| ((|record:a473073e| (|record:a473073e.slot| |variant:fda1d360|))))\n; A variant with the cases refused, start.\n(declare-datatype |variant:c74b9b78| ((|variant:c74b9b78#refused| (|variant:c74b9b78#refused.call| Int) (|variant:c74b9b78#refused.op| String)) (|variant:c74b9b78#start| (|variant:c74b9b78#start.value| Int))))\n\n; Definitions.\n; The invariant, of a state.\n(define-fun |def:invariant| ((|v:state| |record:a473073e|)) Bool (= (ite ((_ is |variant:fda1d360#ok|) (|record:a473073e.slot| |v:state|)) \"ok\" \"waiting\") \"ok\"))\n; The state the step gives.\n(define-fun |def:next| ((|v:state| |record:a473073e|) (|v:input| |variant:c74b9b78|)) |record:a473073e| (let ((|v:n| 1)) (let ((|v:next| (|record:a473073e| (|variant:fda1d360#ok| |v:n|)))) |v:next|)))\n\n; A counterexample to induction.\n(declare-const |q:state| |record:a473073e|)\n(declare-const |q:input| |variant:c74b9b78|)\n(assert (|def:invariant| |q:state|))\n(assert (not (|def:invariant| (|def:next| |q:state| |q:input|))))\n(check-sat)\n(get-value (|q:state| |q:input|))\n"
